.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-DOMAIN-REMOVE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-domain-remove - Stop serving a tunnel at a hostname


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel domain remove <tunnel> <hostname> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Stop serving a tunnel at a hostname

.PP
Stop serving one tunnel at a hostname after confirmation. The workspace domain and its DNS records stay.

.PP
Hostnames come from the workspace's verified domains (pb domain). A hostname is one label under a domain, or the domain itself; the domain's verification and certificate cover it.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	six-character confirmation code from the preview

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for remove

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=2m0s
	maximum time to wait for operation completion

.PP
\fB--wait\fP[=false]
	wait for the operation to reach a terminal state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel-domain(1)\fP
